IMPORT prelude

-- Active Mobility Act 2017 (Singapore) -- which vehicle may be ridden on which kind of path (ss 15, 16, 17), the maximum
-- penalties for the path-conduct offences and who is a repeat offender (ss 2, 15-23C), using a phone while riding (s 22A), the
-- driver's duties after an accident (s 23), and riding under the minimum age and facilitating it (ss 23A, 23B).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/AMA2017.txt, with amendments to
-- Act 5 of 2026 (provisions in force 27 February, 4 May and 1 June 2026) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 12 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the conduct rules a rider of a bicycle,
-- power-assisted bicycle (PAB), personal mobility device (PMD) or mobility vehicle actually meets on a public path. Not encoded:
-- declaring public paths and access agreements (Part 2), rights of passage (ss 12-14), banned and non-compliant vehicles beyond their
-- penalties (ss 18-20), registration marks beyond the penalty (s 20A, Parts 3A, 3B), competency tests and certificates of medical
-- need (Divisions 2A, 2B), codes of conduct, signs and obstruction (ss 24-28), dealing in devices (Part 4), enforcement (Part 5),
-- insurance of hired and employed riders (s 58A), and anything prescribed by regulations -- the speed limits, minimum riding and
-- supervising ages and banned descriptions are all left to regulations, none of which was retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Active Mobility Act 2017 -- conduct on public paths`

-- s 2(1) defines each vehicle. A "bicycle" is built "to be propelled solely by human power"; a PAB is a bicycle "equipped with an
-- electric motor"; a PMD is a wheeled vehicle built to transport people, propelled by an electric motor or human power or both, and
-- "includes a skateboard" but not a bicycle, PAB, motor car, mobility vehicle or wheelchair. A "mobility vehicle" is a mobility
-- scooter, a motorised wheelchair or a prescribed vehicle for someone "unable to walk or has difficulty in walking". A "mechanised
-- sweeper" is a motor vehicle for sweeping or cleansing paths.
DECLARE Vehicle IS ONE OF
    `a bicycle`
    `a power-assisted bicycle`
    `a motorised PMD such as an e-scooter`
    `a non-motorised PMD such as a kick-scooter or skateboard`
    `a mobility vehicle`
    `a mechanised sweeper`
    `a motorcycle or motor car`

-- s 2(1): a "pedestrian-only path" is "provided solely for pedestrians to use"; a "footpath" is "provided for pedestrians to use, or
-- individuals to ride a bicycle or non-motorised personal mobility device on"; a "shared path" is "provided for use by both riders and
-- pedestrians". Each starts and ends at signs, markings, a road or the natural end of the path.
DECLARE PathKind IS ONE OF
    `a pedestrian-only path`
    `a footpath`
    `a shared path`

§§ `15, 16, 17 -- who may ride where`

-- s 15(1): "an individual must not ride a bicycle, a PAB or a personal mobility device, or drive or ride a motor vehicle that is not a
-- mobility vehicle, on a public path that is a pedestrian-only path." (2) Not where the individual riding a bicycle, PAB or PMD is
-- "crossing ... by the shortest safe route" and stays no longer than necessary; or where an adjacent road, footpath or shared path is
-- obstructed, travel there is impracticable, and the individual travels "no more than reasonably necessary" to avoid the obstruction.
-- (3) Not a mechanised sweeper driven "in the course of his or her employment" to clean paths.
--
-- s 16(1): an individual must not "(a) ride a PAB or a motorised personal mobility device on a footpath; or (b) drive on a footpath a
-- motor vehicle that is not a mobility vehicle." (2) The same crossing and obstruction exceptions, for a PAB or motorised PMD only.
-- (3) The same sweeper exception.
--
-- s 17(1): an individual must not "drive or ride on a shared path any motor vehicle that is not a PAB, personal mobility device or
-- mobility vehicle." (2) The sweeper exception. There is no crossing or obstruction exception in s 17.
--
-- A bicycle and a non-motorised PMD are therefore barred only from pedestrian-only paths; a PAB and an e-scooter from pedestrian-only
-- paths and footpaths; a mobility vehicle from none (s 2(1) counts its rider as a "pedestrian").
GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A Vehicle
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the crossing and obstruction exceptions can apply to it` IF
    CONSIDER `the vehicle`
    WHEN `a bicycle` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a power-assisted bicycle` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a motorised PMD such as an e-scooter` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a non-motorised PMD such as a kick-scooter or skateboard` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A Vehicle, `the path` IS A PathKind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the vehicle is barred from the path` IF
    CONSIDER `the path`
    WHEN `a pedestrian-only path` THEN
        CONSIDER `the vehicle`
        WHEN `a mobility vehicle` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    WHEN `a footpath` THEN
        CONSIDER `the vehicle`
        WHEN `a power-assisted bicycle` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a motorised PMD such as an e-scooter` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a mechanised sweeper` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a motorcycle or motor car` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `the vehicle`
        WHEN `a mechanised sweeper` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a motorcycle or motor car` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A Vehicle, `the path` IS A PathKind,
      `crossing by the shortest safe route and staying no longer than necessary` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `avoiding an obstruction on an adjacent area no more than reasonably necessary` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `sweeping paths in the course of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `riding there is an offence` IF
        `the vehicle is barred from the path` `the vehicle` `the path`
    AND NOT (    `the vehicle` EQUALS `a mechanised sweeper` AND `sweeping paths in the course of employment`)
    AND NOT (    `the crossing and obstruction exceptions can apply to it` `the vehicle`
             AND (NOT (`the path` EQUALS `a shared path`))
             AND (   `crossing by the shortest safe route and staying no longer than necessary`
                  OR `avoiding an obstruction on an adjacent area no more than reasonably necessary`))

§§ `2 and Division 2 of Part 3 -- maximum penalties and repeat offenders`

-- s 2(1): a "repeat offender" is a person convicted of an offence who "has been convicted or found guilty of the same offence on at
-- least one other earlier occasion within the period of 5 years immediately before" the current conviction. (ss 16(5), 19(6) and
-- 19A(5) widen "the same offence" to include a pre-3 April 2020 s 16 offence and, for s 19 and s 19A, each other -- not modelled.)
-- The 5-year window is taken as inclusive (AT MOST 5); the text does not settle an earlier conviction exactly 5 years before.
GIVEN `has an earlier conviction for the same offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `years since that earlier conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a repeat offender` IF
    `has an earlier conviction for the same offence` AND `years since that earlier conviction` AT MOST 5

-- The penalty provisions, first offence / repeat offender:
--   s 15(4), 16(4), 17(3) wrong path: $2,000 or 3 months / $5,000 or 6 months
--   s 18(5) banned vehicle: $5,000 or 6 months / $10,000 or 12 months
--   s 19(3) non-compliant vehicle: $10,000 or 6 months / $20,000 or 12 months
--   s 20A(4) registration marks not displayed: $1,000 or 3 months / $2,000 or 6 months
--   s 21(3) speeding: $2,000 or 6 months / $5,000 or 12 months
--   s 22(2) dangerous riding: "$10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months" -- no repeat-offender tier
--   s 22A(2) phone: $1,000 or 3 months / $2,000 or 6 months
--   s 23(3) accident duties: $3,000 or 12 months / $5,000 or 2 years
--   s 23A(2), 23B(2) under-aged riding and facilitating it: $1,000 or 3 months / $2,000 or 6 months
-- Each is "a fine not exceeding ... or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding ... or ... both".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `riding on a barred path`
    `riding a banned vehicle`
    `riding a non-compliant vehicle`
    `not displaying registration marks`
    `speeding`
    `dangerous riding`
    `using a phone while riding`
    `failing in the duties after an injury accident`
    `under-aged riding`
    `facilitating under-aged riding`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `riding on a barred path` THEN (IF `repeat offender` THEN 5000 ELSE 2000)
    WHEN `riding a banned vehicle` THEN (IF `repeat offender` THEN 10000 ELSE 5000)
    WHEN `riding a non-compliant vehicle` THEN (IF `repeat offender` THEN 20000 ELSE 10000)
    WHEN `speeding` THEN (IF `repeat offender` THEN 5000 ELSE 2000)
    WHEN `dangerous riding` THEN 10000
    WHEN `failing in the duties after an injury accident` THEN (IF `repeat offender` THEN 5000 ELSE 3000)
    OTHERWISE (IF `repeat offender` THEN 2000 ELSE 1000)

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `riding on a barred path` THEN (IF `repeat offender` THEN 6 ELSE 3)
    WHEN `riding a banned vehicle` THEN (IF `repeat offender` THEN 12 ELSE 6)
    WHEN `riding a non-compliant vehicle` THEN (IF `repeat offender` THEN 12 ELSE 6)
    WHEN `speeding` THEN (IF `repeat offender` THEN 12 ELSE 6)
    WHEN `dangerous riding` THEN 12
    WHEN `failing in the duties after an injury accident` THEN (IF `repeat offender` THEN 24 ELSE 12)
    OTHERWISE (IF `repeat offender` THEN 6 ELSE 3)

§§ `22A -- mobile communication devices`

-- s 22A(1): the driver or rider of a vehicle "must not hold in his or her hand a mobile communication device and operate any of its
-- communication or other functions, when the vehicle is moving on a public path." (3) "To avoid doubt", it does not apply "(a) to a
-- vehicle or motor vehicle when it is driving itself; or (b) to ... a wearable device (such as a smart watch), when it is worn by the
-- driver or rider in the manner intended by the manufacturer". (4) A "mobile communication device" is a mobile phone or a wireless
-- handheld or wearable device capable of a communication function. Operating "other functions" (a map, music) counts too.
DECLARE PhoneUse HAS
    `holding the device in hand` IS A BOOLEAN
    `operating any of its functions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the vehicle is moving on a public path` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the vehicle is driving itself` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the device is a wearable worn as the manufacturer intended` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the use` IS A PhoneUse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the device is an offence` IF
        `the use`'s `holding the device in hand`
    AND `the use`'s `operating any of its functions`
    AND `the use`'s `the vehicle is moving on a public path`
    AND (NOT `the use`'s `the vehicle is driving itself`)
    AND (NOT `the use`'s `the device is a wearable worn as the manufacturer intended`)

§§ `23 -- duties after an accident`

-- s 23(1): where an accident occurs owing to the presence of a vehicle on a public path and "any individual is injured or any property
-- (including any animal) is damaged or destroyed", the driver must, as far as circumstances permit: (a) "immediately stop"; (b)
-- "immediately render such assistance as he or she can"; (c) give name, residential address, whether insured and the insurer, and the
-- owner's name and address, to the injured person or property owner or their representative; (d) give them to any police officer,
-- authorised officer or public path warden present; (e) if anyone is injured and no officer is present, report in person at the most
-- accessible police station; (f) likewise if property is damaged and neither its owner nor an officer is present.
-- s 23(3): the OFFENCE arises only if "an individual is killed or suffers injury", the driver "knows or ought reasonably to have known"
-- it, and the driver fails to comply with "subsection (1)(a), (b), (c), (d) or (e)". Paragraph (f), and property-only accidents, are
-- outside s 23(3).
DECLARE Accident HAS
    `an individual was killed or injured` IS A BOOLEAN
    `property or an animal was damaged or destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the driver knew or ought reasonably to have known of the death or injury` IS A BOOLEAN
    `stopped immediately` IS A BOOLEAN
    `rendered such assistance as possible` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gave particulars to those affected` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gave particulars to any officer present` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reported the injury at a police station if no officer was present` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reported the property damage at a police station if no one was present` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the accident` IS AN Accident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the driver must comply with section 23(1)` IF
        `the accident`'s `an individual was killed or injured`
    OR  `the accident`'s `property or an animal was damaged or destroyed`

GIVEN `the accident` IS AN Accident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the driver complied with paragraphs (a) to (e)` IF
        `the accident`'s `stopped immediately`
    AND `the accident`'s `rendered such assistance as possible`
    AND `the accident`'s `gave particulars to those affected`
    AND `the accident`'s `gave particulars to any officer present`
    AND `the accident`'s `reported the injury at a police station if no officer was present`

GIVEN `the accident` IS AN Accident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the driver commits the section 23(3) offence` IF
        `the accident`'s `an individual was killed or injured`
    AND `the accident`'s `the driver knew or ought reasonably to have known of the death or injury`
    AND (NOT `the driver complied with paragraphs (a) to (e)` `the accident`)

§§ `23A, 23B -- under-aged riding of motorised PMDs on shared paths`

-- s 23A(1): an individual "commits an offence if the individual rides a motorised personal mobility device on a shared path when he or
-- she is below the prescribed minimum riding age". (3) Not where riding "under escort by one or more appropriate supervisors (whether
-- or not a parent or guardian)". (4) An "appropriate supervisor" has "attained a minimum supervising age prescribed"; "riding under
-- escort" means (a) by arrangement, a supervisor "on or in the vicinity of the shared path" and (b) riding so that the supervisor "has
-- a clear and unobstructed line of sight". (5) The ages are prescribed by regulations; here they are inputs.
DECLARE Escort HAS
    `the supervisor's age` IS A NUMBER
    `the prescribed minimum supervising age` IS A NUMBER
    `escort arranged for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the supervisor is on or near the shared path` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the supervisor has a clear line of sight` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the escort` IS AN Escort
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rider is riding under escort` IF
        `the escort`'s `the supervisor's age` AT LEAST `the escort`'s `the prescribed minimum supervising age`
    AND `the escort`'s `escort arranged for the purpose`
    AND `the escort`'s `the supervisor is on or near the shared path`
    AND `the escort`'s `the supervisor has a clear line of sight`

GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A Vehicle, `the path` IS A PathKind, `rider age` IS A NUMBER, `prescribed minimum riding age` IS A NUMBER,
      `the escort` IS AN Escort
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rider commits the under-aged riding offence` IF
        `the vehicle` EQUALS `a motorised PMD such as an e-scooter`
    AND `the path` EQUALS `a shared path`
    AND `rider age` LESS THAN `prescribed minimum riding age`
    AND (NOT `the rider is riding under escort` `the escort`)

-- s 23B(1): a person commits an offence if (a) the person "invites, allows or facilitates" an individual below the minimum riding age
-- to ride a motorised PMD on a shared path; (b) knows or is negligent as to whether BOTH the individual is under age AND is not escorted
-- by an appropriate supervisor; and (c) the individual does so ride. (4) "facilitate" requires intent or recklessness and "excludes
-- mere advertising and selling (but not letting for hire)". (3) Defence, proved on a balance of probabilities: reasonable grounds to
-- believe and reasonable inquiries that the rider was not under age, or reasonably accepting evidence from the rider that he or she was
-- not. The intent-or-recklessness element belongs to "facilitate" in (4); it is not applied here to inviting or allowing.
DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `inviting the child to ride`
    `allowing the child to ride`
    `lending the device`
    `letting the device for hire`
    `merely selling the device`
    `merely advertising the device`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct can be inviting, allowing or facilitating` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `merely selling the device` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `merely advertising the device` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE Facilitation HAS
    `the conduct` IS A Conduct
    `intended or reckless that it would enable the riding` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew or was negligent that the child was under age and unescorted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child did ride a motorised PMD on a shared path under age` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made reasonable inquiries on reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonably accepted evidence of age from the rider` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the case` IS A Facilitation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the facilitation offence` IF
        `the conduct can be inviting, allowing or facilitating` (`the case`'s `the conduct`)
    AND (    `the case`'s `intended or reckless that it would enable the riding`
         OR  `the case`'s `the conduct` EQUALS `inviting the child to ride`
         OR  `the case`'s `the conduct` EQUALS `allowing the child to ride`)
    AND `the case`'s `knew or was negligent that the child was under age and unescorted`
    AND `the case`'s `the child did ride a motorised PMD on a shared path under age`
    AND (NOT `the case`'s `made reasonable inquiries on reasonable grounds`)
    AND (NOT `the case`'s `reasonably accepted evidence of age from the rider`)
